    "narration_segments": [
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-1",
        "stage_id": "step1",
        "component_id": "comp-step1-welcome",
        "ssml": "<speak>Let's Learn Subtraction with Borrowing! Today we will learn how to subtract big numbers by borrowing from our neighbour, just like sharing rupees or apples.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-2",
        "stage_id": "step2",
        "component_id": "comp-step2-visualillustration",
        "ssml": "<speak>Borrowing a ten to help subtract.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-3",
        "stage_id": "step3",
        "component_id": "comp-step3-storynarration",
        "ssml": "<speak>Imagine you have 45 apples in a basket and you give 27 apples to your friend. How many apples are left? We need to borrow to find the answer.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-4",
        "stage_id": "step4",
        "component_id": "comp-step4-guidedexamplepanel",
        "ssml": "<speak>Example: 45 minus 27. Look at the ones: 5 is less than 7, so borrow 1 ten from the 4 tens. The 4 tens become 3 tens, and the ones become 15. Subtract the ones: 15 minus 7 equals 8. Subtract the tens: 3 minus 2 equals 1. Answer: 18.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-5",
        "stage_id": "step5",
        "component_id": "comp-step5-practiceinput",
        "ssml": "<speak>Solve: 53 minus 28 equals question mark.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-6",
        "stage_id": "step5",
        "component_id": "comp-step5-hintbutton",
        "ssml": "<speak>Remember to borrow from the tens if the top ones digit is smaller.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-7",
        "stage_id": "step6",
        "component_id": "comp-step6-practiceinput",
        "ssml": "<speak>Solve: 64 minus 39 equals question mark.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-8",
        "stage_id": "step7",
        "component_id": "comp-step7-hintbutton",
        "ssml": "<speak>Remember to borrow from the tens if the top ones digit is smaller.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-9",
        "stage_id": "step8",
        "component_id": "comp-step8-mistakehighlight",
        "ssml": "<speak>A common mistake is to subtract the smaller number from the larger one in each column without borrowing. Always start with the ones column and borrow when needed.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-10",
        "stage_id": "step9",
        "component_id": "comp-step9-challengepanel",
        "ssml": "<speak>Challenge: If you have 82 marbles and you lose 47, how many marbles do you have left? Show your borrowing steps.</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-11",
        "stage_id": "step10",
        "component_id": "comp-step10-summarycard",
        "ssml": "<speak>Today we learned how to borrow from the tens column to subtract two-digit numbers. Remember to check your work by adding!</speak>",
        "timing_map": {},
        "highlight_map": {},
        "pronunciation_overrides": {}
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "seg-12",
        "stage_id": "step11",
        "component_id": "comp-step11-quiz",
        "ssml": "<speak>Question 1: In 53 minus 28, what do you do first? Option A: Subtract 3-8 directly Option B: Borrow 1 ten from the 5 tens Option C: Subtract 5-2 first Option D: Add the numbers Question 2: What is 64 minus 39? Option A: 25 Option B: 35 Option C: 24 Option D: 15 Question 3: When you borrow 1 ten, you add blank ones to the ones column.</speak>",
